@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple SysML Parametric Diagram with one constraint block F = m*a binding a parameter to a value property.
'   usecase:      Teach constraint block, constraint parameters, and binding connectors (equality).
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       physics
' ============================================================================
title Example Parametric - Simple F = m*a

note top of "NewtonLaw"
  PARAMETRIC DIAGRAM NOTE:
  Edges here are BINDING CONNECTORS (==).
  A binding means the two ends are EQUAL
  (same value), NOT that material flows.
end note

class "NewtonLaw" <<constraint>> {
  { F = m * a }
}

package "Binding context (inside a DynamicBody block)" {
  object "F : Force" as Fp
  object "m : Mass" as mp
  object "a : Acceleration" as ap

  class "NewtonLawInst" as "fma : NewtonLaw" <<constraint>> {
    }
}

Fp == fma
mp == fma
ap == fma

note right of fma
  The constraint block exposes PARAMETERS
  (F, m, a). Each value property of the
  enclosing block is bound (==) to a
  parameter port, making them equal and
  enforcing the equation F = m*a.
end note

@enduml
